[# Section 7 — tooling: CLI, editors, LSP, tree-sitter.
   Cross-refs tooling/* dirs + scripts/gen_docs + docs/playground. #]

[section id=tooling n=7 title='Tooling'

  [child id=cli n=7.1 title='The cx CLI'
    [intro
      """`cx` is the one-stop command-line interface. It parses, evaluates,
         validates, converts, formats, hashes, and lints CX documents.
         Built from the same V codebase as libcx, so every binding sees
         identical behavior."""]

    [body
      """The most common subcommands:"""]

    [table columns=(command, purpose)
      [row command='cx parse FILE' purpose='Parse and pretty-print']
      [row command='cx canon FILE' purpose='Emit canonical bytes']
      [row command='cx hash FILE' purpose='Print SHA-256 of canonical bytes']
      [row command='cx eval FILE CODE' purpose='Evaluate code against document']
      [row command='cx select FILE CXPATH' purpose='CXPath query']
      [row command='cx modify FILE CXPATH ACTION' purpose='Pure-functional update']
      [row command='cx convert FILE --to FORMAT' purpose='Project to JSON/YAML/TOML/XML/MD']
      [row command='cx validate FILE --schema FILE.cxs' purpose='Schema validation']
      [row command='cx fmt FILE' purpose='Pretty-print (preserves comments)']
      [row command='cx lint FILE' purpose='Style + correctness lints']
      [row command='cx diff A B' purpose='Structural diff']]

    [example lang=cx
      """$ cx select users.cx '//user[@active=true]/@email'
         ada@example.com
         linus@example.com

         $ cx modify users.cx '//user[@id=1]/@name' --set Alice
         [users [user :id 1 :name 'Alice' +active] ...]

         $ cx hash users.cx
         3a7bd3e2360a9f12...."""]

    [note
      """Run `cx --help` for the full subcommand list. The CLI is itself
         conformance-tested — fixtures under `conformance/cli.txt` lock
         the surface."""]]

  [child id=editors n=7.2 title='Editor integration'
    [intro
      """CX ships first-class editor support for VS Code, Neovim, Helix,
         and any editor that consumes LSP and tree-sitter. Tooling lives
         under `tooling/`; the install scripts under `tooling/install/`
         set everything up."""]

    [list
      [item """**VS Code** — install the `cx-language` extension
              (`tooling/vscode/`). Provides syntax highlight, snippets,
              LSP-backed diagnostics, hover, completion, jump-to-def."""]
      [item """**Neovim** — see `tooling/neovim/README.md`. Uses
              `nvim-treesitter` + the bundled LSP server."""]
      [item """**Helix** — language definition snippets in
              `tooling/helix.example.toml`; tree-sitter grammar
              from `tooling/tree-sitter-cx/`."""]
      [item """**Any LSP client** — the language server binary is
              `tooling/lsp/` built; speaks LSP 3.17 over stdio."""]]]

  [child id=lsp n=7.3 title='Language server (LSP)'
    [intro
      """The LSP server provides the same intelligence to every editor
         that speaks LSP. Implementation: `tooling/lsp/` (V binary)."""]

    [body
      """Capabilities:"""]

    [list
      [item """**Diagnostics.** Parser errors, schema violations, error
              codes from `cx lint`, unreachable `[?match]` arms, missing
              `:else` hints, `:where` consolidation suggestions."""]
      [item """**Hover.** Element schema info, attribute types,
              directive documentation, **CXPath focus hover** showing
              match-count + axis docs (new in v0.8.0)."""]
      [item """**Completion.** Element names from schema, attribute names,
              directive names, **CXPath axis names + node-kind tests**."""]
      [item """**Definition / references.** Across `[?cx include]`
              boundaries — go-to-def follows include resolution."""]
      [item """**Layer-2 explain.** Hovering a Layer-2 host idiom
              (Python comprehension, Go filter chain, Rust iterator)
              shows the desugared Layer-1 form. Implementation calls
              `cxlib.idioms.explain()` (see [[layer-2]])."""]
      [item """**`[?modify]` focus type check.** Static error when
              `:set-attr` / `:delete-attr` target an attribute-step
              path (per ADR
              [0030](../../spec/decisions/0030-modify-pure-functional-updates.md) D7)."""]]]

  [child id=tree-sitter n=7.4 title='Tree-sitter grammar'
    [intro
      """`tooling/tree-sitter-cx/` is the tree-sitter grammar for CX.
         Used by VS Code, Neovim, Helix, GitHub syntax highlight, and any
         tree-sitter consumer."""]

    [body
      """The grammar covers everything in [`spec/grammar.ebnf`](../../spec/grammar.ebnf):
         elements, attributes, scalars, sigils, collection literals, all
         39 directives, CXPath path expressions (`//`, `/`, 12 axes,
         predicates, `AttrTest`), multi-arm `[?match]` slots
         (`:case` / `:when` / `:else` / `_`), and `[?modify]` action
         slots."""]

    [body
      """Highlight queries live in
         `tooling/tree-sitter-cx/queries/highlights.scm`; injection
         queries (for embedded other-language code blocks) in
         `queries/injections.scm`."""]

    [note
      """The `make tree-sitter` target rebuilds the parser binary; the
         CI gate keeps it in sync with `spec/grammar.ebnf`."""]]]
